<article class="env-lemma" id="041R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/041R">Lemma <span data-tag="041R">74.11.7</span>.</a> The property $\mathcal{P}(f) =$“$f$ is universally injective” is fpqc local on the base. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We will use Lemma <a href="/tag/041J" data-tag="041J">74.10.4</a> to prove this. Assumptions (1) and (2) of that lemma follow from Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03IT" data-tag="03IT">67.9.5</a>. Let $Z' \to Z$ be a flat surjective morphism of affine schemes over $S$ and let $f : X \to Z$ be a morphism from an algebraic space to $Z$. Assume that the base change $f' : X' \to Z'$ is universally injective. Let $K$ be a field, and let $a, b : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K) \to X$ be two morphisms such that $f \circ a = f \circ b$. As $Z' \to Z$ is surjective there exists a field extension $K'/K$ and a morphism $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K') \to Z'$ such that the following solid diagram commutes 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K') \ar[rrd] \ar@{-->}[rd]_{a', b'} \ar[dd] \\  &  X' \ar[r] \ar[d] &  Z' \ar[d] \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K) \ar[r]^{a, b} &  X \ar[r] &  Z }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       As the square is cartesian we get the two dotted arrows $a'$, $b'$ making the diagram commute. Since $X' \to Z'$ is universally injective we get $a' = b'$. This forces $a = b$ as $\{ \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K') \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K)\} $ is an fpqc covering, see Properties of Spaces, Proposition <a href="/tag/0APL" data-tag="0APL">66.17.1</a>. Hence $f$ is universally injective as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>